From 2af5f05ccb6f0e2b8ea4631538983cefad706312 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Tcelishchev <casualuser@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:25:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(border,actions): add 8-zone window snapping with
 top-half edge default

Add E_MAXIMIZE_TOP and E_MAXIMIZE_BOTTOM directions alongside existing quarter zones so windows can snap to all 4 screen halves (left, right, top, bottom) and all 4 corner quarters via both mouse drag and Super+Arrow keybindings.

Default top-edge center drag to Top Half (E_MAXIMIZE_TOP) rather than Full Maximize so all four edges and four corners behave symmetrically, while preserving an opt-in 'Maximize fully when dragging to top edge' setting in Window Geometry (and keeping titlebar double-click, Maximize button, and double Super+Up for Full Maximize). Also clear bd->maximized transiently across zone transitions when allow_manip is disabled and restore X/Y cursor alignment when unsnapping.
